From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:54:42 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(delegate): a message to a waiting subagent wakes it at
 once

A subagent that ended its turn waiting on a background job (patch 0092)
has no next tool result, so a steer, an agent_send message or the hub's
Send sat queued until the job exited, hours later. delegate_task's steer
said "queued" and the subagent looked dead.

A steer to a waiting subagent now wakes it at once with the text as its
next input, plus a note that its job is still running (command and elapsed
time). The watch stays armed and the subagent ends its turn waiting again.
Messages sent together are read in order in one wake; a message that
arrives with the job's exit joins that wake. delegate_task and
subagent.steer answer "delivered" instead of "queued". Stop on a waiting
subagent wakes its wait loop immediately.
